description:
Stage 1 - Expression of Interest

The Council is seeking Submissions from suitably qualified and experienced Respondents for the design and construction of the Works, which include the design, construction, commissioning and handover of upgrade works at the Plant and associated raw water pump station.

In particular, the Works include, but are not limited to:

* installation of a validated ultraviolet disinfection process as a second barrier against chlorine-resistant pathogens, including a new UV building or enclosure and associated civil, mechanical, electrical and control works;

* provision of dedicated powder activated carbon contact time upstream of the treatment process, including a new PAC contact tank and associated PAC storage, batching and dosing facilities;

* replacement and upgrade of chemical storage, batching and dosing systems, including potassium permanganate, soda ash, liquid alum and chlorine, with modern, automated and bunded installations;

* raw water flow control improvements at the raw water pump station;

* sedimentation tank sludge removal upgrades;

* filter-to-waste improvements;

* improved site lighting;

* upgrade of supporting site services, including chemical delivery access, power, service water, chemical wastewater containment and stormwater, required to support the new process and dosing systems;

* process pipework, valves, flow meters, pits, access platforms and associated civil works;

* electrical, instrumentation, control and automation works, including integration with the existing Plant control system;

* temporary works, bypassing, staging and shutdown planning required to maintain continuous production of compliant drinking water;

* testing, commissioning, performance proving, operator training and handover; and

* preparation and submission of required design and construction documentation, including quality records, testing and commissioning records, as-constructed information and operation and maintenance manuals.

The Works will be undertaken within a live and operational water treatment plant and raw water pump station. They will require careful staging, temporary works and commissioning strategies so that compliant drinking water supply is maintained throughout their performance.

An indicative description of the Works and the Council’s other requirements is included in Part 2.

Stage 2 - Request for Tender

Successful Respondents (if any) from Stage 1 will be invited to participate in the RFT (separate VP#), which will specifically detail the Council's technical, contractual and commercial requirements.

